WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
And what many feared

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.602
would be a night of violence

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:03.737
was largely peaceful,

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:04.437
with protests

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.639
across the country in New York.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.041
Three people were arrested,

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.010
one for breaking the windshield

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:10.777
of a patrol car.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:11.911
But overall,

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.513
what we saw were calm

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:16.149
and peaceful protests

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:17.684
Amara.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.718
I want to bring in CNN's

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:19.552
Sara Sidner

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:21.788
to this conversation here in Memphis.

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.723
And Sara, you spent the night

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.691
with protesters.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.993
You visited the scene where we watched

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.561
that horrible video

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.497
where all of that unfolded

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:32.098
when you were with the protesters.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.333
They got on the interstate.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:34.634
What were they sharing with you?

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.702
What were they calling for?

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.302
You know,

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.138
they wanted people to see them

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.973
and see what had happened here

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.841
and make sure that

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.576
the community, not just here,

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.111
but around the country, understood

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.147
that there is a problem with policing

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:49.249
and that they wanted to see changes.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.450
And they talked about

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.851
whether or not they were

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.220
satisfied.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:54.754
I guess, if

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.657
you will, with the charges, satisfied

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:58.792
with the response

00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.793
from the police department

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.461
for the firings of the officers,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.129
which came very swiftly,

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.798
and then these charges,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.398
which included

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.866
second degree murder,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.868
aggravated kidnaping, aggravated assault.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:09.869
But, you know,

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.438
when they saw the video,

00:01:11.438 --> 00:01:13.606
they just felt there's so much more

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.542
that has happened before this

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.843
that could have stopped this.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.812
And so they're unsatisfied

00:01:18.812 --> 00:01:20.413
with what has happened here.

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.382
I know everyone has been praising

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.751
the police chief and praising the D.A.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:25.785
for going forward

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:26.653
with charges so quickly,

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:27.787
because that is unusual.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:28.988
And we've seen many cases

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:30.924
where it's taken up to a year

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:31.858
for anything to happen

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.193
and sometimes nothing at all.

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:34.561
But when they saw the video

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:35.995
and they knowing what has happened

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.596
to some of them

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.064
in the past with their interactions

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:39.699
with police, they were unsatisfied.

00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:40.233
They said this

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.668
should never have happened.

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.303
And because things weren't done

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.038
before this happened,

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:45.972
to some of these units,

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:47.707
like the Scorpio unit,

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.008
we have this situation

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:52.011
where a 29 year old who was a free

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:54.013
spirit ends up losing his life.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:55.315
So there was anger,

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.216
there was frustration,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.617
there was a lot of pain,

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:58.852
but there was no destruction.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:01:59.986
There was no violence.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.421
They disrupted traffic.

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:04.224
They moved on after an hour or so.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:05.692
And that was the end of it.

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.093
It has been a very peaceful,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:09.796
mostly prayerful time here in Memphis.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.398
But they want to see major reforms

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.001
and they want to see it now.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.369
And the family's

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.370
attorney, Ben Crump,

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.037
pointed out

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:19.606
that only a few days

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.708
before the incident with Tyree,

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.143
another person in this community

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:23.943
had complained

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.111
about that

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.912
Scorpion unit

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:27.614
saying that they had used excessive

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.249
force on him.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.416
What is the sense that you're

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.751
getting from the community

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.086
and from leaders in the community

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:35.622
about how likely change is to come?

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:37.023
Well, we're getting a clue

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.224
when it comes to particularly

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.692
the Scorpion unit.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.127
The police chief

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.363
has basically put that unit on hold.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.697
The unit was put in place

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.199
for crime suppression.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:46.666
The family

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.433
and their attorneys say

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:50.403
it turned into oppression of citizens.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:51.437
They were just sort of

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.439
after people in their minds

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.241
looking for people as

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:55.942
suspects

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.178
instead of looking at people as citizens.

00:02:58.811 --> 00:02:59.913
And so right now,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.181
that has been put on hold.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:02.882
What the family is asking for

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.184
is that and their attorneys

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:06.386
is that they disband this

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.921
group altogether.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.189
Whether or not that will happen,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:09.923
we do not know.

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.791
But there is sort of an investigation

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.826
they put on hold underway

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:16.296
and you may see more people either

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.597
lose their jobs

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:18.998
or be put on administrative leave

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:20.567
beside those two sheriff's deputies,

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.002
because I think we counted more than nine

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.704
people who were out there at the time.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:26.105
There's also the question

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.641
that sticks in everyone's mind,

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:30.243
the fire members of the fire

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.177
department who were there.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:34.647
They are they're not as law enforcement.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:38.351
They are there to save lives and help.

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.487
And if that's not what they did

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:45.558
and just sit around then that is why

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:46.459
they have

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.293
been, you know,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.027
sort of

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.095
they haven't been fired yet

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:49.729
because they have to go

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:50.663
through a process.

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.699
But there is a lot of questions,

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:54.334
sort of the duty to intervene

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:55.868
and the duty to do their work

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.203
to try to save someone.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.371
So there's a lot of questions here.

00:03:58.371 --> 00:03:58.871
Imagine

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.506
you're a person going through this

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.808
and the people sent there to

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:04.844
to to be the rescue do nothing.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.647
That really hurt a lot of people as well.

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.282
It was one of the most painful parts

00:04:09.282 --> 00:04:11.251
of watching all of that footage

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.453
that as they're holding on to him

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.087
and beating him

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.421
when he presents, no threat

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:16.990
to any of the officers around him.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.091
Nobody intervenes.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.492
And then he's just slumped over

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.060
and it appears negligent.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.595
It appears that they're not

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.763
actually tending to him

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.965
as they're talking about what happened.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:27.333
Sir, I'm curious

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.501
to get your perspective on this,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:29.702
because as we noted before

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.371
and we were talking to

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:32.872
defense attorney Shan Wu earlier

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.473
this morning,

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.542
he makes the case that

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:37.844
there was nothing in the footage

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.479
that shows

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.247
a provocation

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:42.181
or a threat

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.816
that Tyree poses at any moment.

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.550
In fact,

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.352
if this was a traffic stop,

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.387
why are they pulling him

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.689
out of the car to begin with? Right.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.591
Have you gotten any indication

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.059
from perhaps

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:53.926
law enforcement

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.228
or from defense attorneys

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.330
that there might be some explanation

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:58.798
for how aggravated

00:04:58.798 --> 00:04:59.432
the officers

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.267
were as they approached the scene?

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.135
The simple answer to

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.637
that is no from the D.A.,

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.372
no from the police.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.940
They have not found evidence

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.776
leading up to this

00:05:09.776 --> 00:05:11.911
to in any way, shape or form

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:15.014
that there was a reckless driving

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:18.551
and be any reason for this to get so hot

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:21.120
so fast and be so aggressive.

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.089
What you do hear on the tape

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:24.290
is officers sound

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.291
very angry

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.392
when they pepper spray

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:27.593
because the pepper spray blows

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:28.761
back in their face

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.864
and they blame it on Tyree Nichols.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.066
Not on themselves.

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.801
The ones that sprayed the pepper spray

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:35.835
so close up,

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.770
they blame it both to officers.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.138
You hear them blaming

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.306
Terry Nichols for this.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.842
So you could hear the sort of swell,

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:43.776
the heightened emotions.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.244
And one person described

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:47.080
this as in their minds,

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:49.082
they looked like a pack of wolves.

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:50.850
The group mentality happened.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.685
There was a gang mentality that happened.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:56.089
And they just all of them in a fury

00:05:56.222 --> 00:05:57.256
went after him.

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:58.558
And you can hear him saying

00:05:58.558 --> 00:05:59.859
you're doing too much, like,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:00.793
what are you doing?

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:01.394
What did I do

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:02.795
when he's screaming for his mother?

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:03.796
And this will sit with me

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:04.731
for the rest of my life

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.499
when he's screaming for his mom

00:06:06.499 --> 00:06:08.301
and saying it over and over again,

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:10.169
she's about 80 yards away.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:10.870
She said

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.271
And she truly believes

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:15.274
he actually was hoping she could hear him

00:06:15.575 --> 00:06:16.309
and she couldn't

00:06:16.309 --> 00:06:18.478
be there for her son in his last moments.

00:06:18.478 --> 00:06:20.780
And that will never leave her mind.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:21.681
And she said,

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:23.449
I don't even know how to process that.

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.218
And who would. Right.

00:06:25.218 --> 00:06:26.085
Before we go, Sara,

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:26.986
I just want to make sure

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.321
that for our viewers

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.123
who have watched that footage,

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:31.023
it's agonizing

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.759
but we do want to share

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.694
who Tyree Nichols was

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:36.229
and paint him in a different light

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:37.997
than just the person that the victim

00:06:37.997 --> 00:06:39.665
that you see in that footage.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.234
You mentioned that he was a free spirit.

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.201
His mom talks about him

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:43.102
being a photographer

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:45.071
who like to photograph sunsets.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.906
She said that he was a skater.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.541
What else stands out to you

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.575
when you hear those details

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:50.343
from his family?

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:51.310
You know, we went and looked.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.745
He has a photography site

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:53.913
where he would

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.381
regularly go out

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:57.750
and take beautiful pictures of Memphis.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.986
But when the sun is setting

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.488
and they are beautiful pictures, he

00:07:02.522 --> 00:07:03.823
that was his passion.

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:05.258
He was working at FedEx.

00:07:05.258 --> 00:07:06.426
He was working, by the way,

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:07.493
with his father.

00:07:07.493 --> 00:07:08.995
They both worked at FedEx.

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.563
And the thing that also stuck with me

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.331
is that he would come home

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.367
almost every night for dinner

00:07:14.367 --> 00:07:15.435
with his family.

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:17.570
He'd walk in and say, hi, family.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:19.405
And she says, I'll never hear that again.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.406
And I don't know how to live with that.

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:22.942
That is

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.111
such a painful note.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:26.712
Sara, thank you so much.

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:27.146
We know

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.481
there might be demonstrations later.

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:30.016
So look forward to your reporting

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:30.683
on that.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.218
Always appreciate being on site for us.

